---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Approach">
<section class="approach-v53"><div class="container">
<header class="simple-page-head"><div class="eyebrow">Approach</div><h1>Understand. Design. Implement. Improve.</h1><p>A practical cycle for turning ambiguity into systems people can actually use.</p></header>
<div class="approach-sequence">
<article class="approach-unit reveal"><div class="system-art"><svg viewBox="0 0 260 150"><path d="M8 24C58 24 72 67 126 70S190 45 250 72"/><path d="M8 46C60 46 76 76 126 78S191 62 250 78"/><path d="M8 68C62 68 78 85 126 86S193 79 250 84"/><path d="M8 91C60 91 79 94 126 94S194 96 250 91"/><circle cx="28" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="53" cy="46" r="3"/><circle cx="77" cy="68" r="3"/><circle class="accent-fill" cx="126" cy="82" r="7"/></svg></div><div class="step-no">01</div><h2>Understand</h2><p>Listen, observe, map the current state, and identify the problem worth solving.</p></article>
<article class="approach-unit reveal"><div class="system-art"><svg viewBox="0 0 260 150"><path d="M28 122V32H118"/><path d="M52 122V55H143"/><path d="M77 122V79H167"/><circle cx="145" cy="50" r="34"/><circle class="accent-fill" cx="178" cy="87" r="25"/><path class="fine" d="M118 17v112M16 101h211"/></svg></div><div class="step-no">02</div><h2>Design</h2><p>Connect insights, define structure, and shape a system around what the work actually needs.</p></article>
<article class="approach-unit reveal"><div class="system-art"><svg viewBox="0 0 260 150"><path d="M35 77L78 42l49 38 43-45 54 49"/><path d="M78 42v72M127 80v37M170 35v77"/><circle cx="35" cy="77" r="8"/><circle class="accent-fill" cx="78" cy="42" r="10"/><circle cx="127" cy="80" r="11"/><circle class="sage-fill" cx="170" cy="35" r="12"/><circle cx="224" cy="84" r="9"/><rect x="68" y="104" width="20" height="20"/><rect class="accent-fill" x="117" y="107" width="20" height="20"/><rect x="160" y="102" width="20" height="20"/></svg></div><div class="step-no">03</div><h2>Implement</h2><p>Bring the system into practice through collaboration, documentation, enablement, and ownership.</p></article>
<article class="approach-unit reveal"><div class="system-art"><svg viewBox="0 0 260 150"><path d="M32 96C48 32 116 18 158 49s20 79-22 76-56-44-24-62 71-5 111 27"/><path class="accent" d="M203 78l21 12-20 14"/><circle class="sage-fill" cx="32" cy="96" r="6"/><circle class="accent-fill" cx="158" cy="49" r="7"/><path class="fine" d="M52 115C83 137 133 139 172 120"/></svg></div><div class="step-no">04</div><h2>Improve</h2><p>Measure what changed, learn from use, and refine the system so it keeps creating value.</p></article>
</div>
<div class="approach-working-style reveal">
  <div class="eyebrow">How I Work With People</div>
  <div class="working-style-grid">
    <div><h3>Collaborate from the start.</h3><p>I involve the people closest to the work early, because the strongest solutions come from combining their experience with a broader view of the system. I want people participating in the solution, not simply receiving one.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Create clarity together.</h3><p>I turn complex problems into shared language, clear priorities, and practical next steps so teams understand not only what we're changing, but why.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Coach, enable, and build ownership.</h3><p>My leadership style is collaborative and coaching-oriented. I focus on giving people context, developing their judgment, and creating enough structure for them to succeed without needing constant direction.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
